    {# The LocalBusiness reviews/aggregateRating block was removed 2026-08-06
       (Lee's ruling, code-refresh D7): Google's review-snippet policy makes
       self-serving reviews — reviews embedded in an entity's markup on its
       own site — ineligible and a manual-action risk, and anonymous "Private
       Client" authors compounded it. The testimonials remain as visible page
       copy on the homepage, which is fine; only the structured-data wrapper
       was against policy. If real attributable reviews ever back it (Google
       Business Profile), that lives on GBP, not here. #}

    <!-- Favicon -->
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/img/favicon-64.png">

    <!-- Preload.
         `hero_image` WINS over `preload_image` where both exist, and that
         ordering is the fix for a real regression (2026-09-02). The five
         service-area pages state their hero twice: `hero_image` renders the
         background, `preload_image` was a hand-written absolute path meant to
         name the same file. The 2026-08-10 photo reassignment changed the first
         and not the second, so north-shore, sea-to-sky and whistler preloaded a
         1920w hero belonging to another page -- fetching ~267KB at highest
         priority that no element ever draws, while the hero that DOES draw got
         no preload at all. Deriving it from the same field that renders it means
         the two cannot disagree again. Pages with no `hero_image` (home, about,
         faq, contact, locations, saunas, warranty) are unaffected. -->
    {% if hero_image %}
    <link rel="preload" as="image" href="/img/{{ hero_image }}-1920w.webp">
    {% elif preload_image %}
    <link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ preload_image }}">
    {% endif %}

    <!-- Fonts: self-hosted, so no Google origins and no third-party round trip.
         The two Google preconnects and the Google CSS <link> are gone; the CSP
         lost both origins with them.

         Preload EXACTLY these two: the above-the-fold pair. The Cormorant
         italic and nothing else are deliberately not preloaded -- they are
         below the fold on every entry page, and preloading them would compete
         with the LCP hero image for bandwidth.

         Filenames are content-hashed, so `crossorigin` is required (fonts are
         always fetched in anonymous CORS mode; without it the preload is
         discarded and the file is fetched twice). -->
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/cormorant-garamond-var.16b298e9dcfa.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/outfit-var.55112282293d.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>

    <!-- External Stylesheet -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/styles.css' | assetUrl }}">

    <!-- Leaflet.js for Maps - lazy loaded when locations page is visited -->
</head>
